Usage: raphael favorite <path> [options]
       raphael favorite --id <id> [options]

Add an area or project to favorites.

Already a favorite succeeds without a change. Favorites keep their state while
archived; favorites leaves archived items out unless --include-archived is
given.

Options:
      --id <id>
          Address by stable id instead of path.
      --json
          Print the result as one JSON document.
  -h, --help
          Show help.

Examples:
  raphael favorite /work
  raphael favorite --id 42
  raphael favorite /work/raphael --json

Prints:
  The item with its path and favorite state; Unchanged when it already was in
  that state. JSON carries `nodeId`, `isFavorite`, `changed` and `node`.

Next: raphael favorites

See also: raphael help unfavorite

