Usage: raphael get <path> [options]
       raphael get --id <id> [options]

Read one item and its current revision.

Read one area, project, or note, including its body, tags, metadata and archive
causes. Markdown export is best effort; see `raphael help content`.

Options:
      --id <id>
          Address by stable id instead of path.
      --return-format <format>
          Returned body: markdown or tiptap. Requires --json. Default: markdown.
      --json
          Print the result as one JSON document.
  -h, --help
          Show help.

Examples:
  raphael get /work/raphael/api-design
  raphael get --id 42
  raphael get --id 42 --return-format tiptap --json

Prints:
  Every field, including path, revision and update time, then the body. JSON
  carries `entity`.

Next: raphael update --id 42 --title "Reviewed design"

See also: raphael help content; raphael help revisions

